# Finite mask lists for the max2 fiber forest

These lists are witnesses only. This module certifies their lengths and the
resulting bounds on sets of listed masks. It does not assert that a coordinate
is square-one or conjugate to the proposed representative. Those assertions
are the independent orbit-forest certificate.

The lists use the shared Representatives bit convention. They were discovered
from the original ATLAS max2 matrices; provenance and reproduction instructions
are in FiberCensus/source/README.md. The census motivation is
Aschbacher--Smith, refs/quasithin.pdf, printed pp.64--65, A.6.1--4.
-/

